Glass Thickness and Via Diameter Influence Product Development

Substrate thickness and via dimensions are important technical considerations in TGV manufacturing. These parameters influence electrical interconnection design, fabrication complexity and application suitability.

The report evaluates glass thickness categories below 100 µm, 100–300 µm and above 300 µm. Via diameter is segmented into below 30 µm, 30–100 µm and above 100 µm.

These classifications provide insight into the different engineering requirements across advanced packaging applications.

Asia-Pacific Leads the TGV Substrate Market

Asia-Pacific held the largest regional position in 2025. The region benefits from established semiconductor manufacturing and advanced packaging activities across Japan, South Korea, China and Taiwan.

Its semiconductor packaging ecosystem and substrate manufacturing capabilities provide a strong foundation for TGV adoption. The region also has the strongest growth profile over the forecast period.

